t about  rogers the is the um  is the uh what i described as the sort  of miracle of what's happened in the  north of ireland over  uh  the the the lifetime of my generation so  from 30 years of um  dark and tragic trouble through 25 years  of this very hard-earned very fragile  piece which began with what we are  struggling to see at the moment which is  the very very very difficult thing  of trying to begin the process of  understanding  first of all listening to people with  whom you profoundly disagree and finding  a way to listen  understand respect and possibly accept  on the road to progress it's incredibly  easy to say it's unbelievably hard to do  and yet that's where progress is made in  in in the whole of ireland there was a a  generation of people ready to do that  and the example of the last 25 years as  fragile as it remains is still a shining  light in the darkness and it's one that  i would say we want to try and see  shining as quickly as possible in other  situations in the world where  what seems to be the impossible can be  possible and and it is it is  unbelievably difficult and unbelievably  necessary and and um what i see across  my lifetime is an incredible effort made  that has been worth it but please god  situations in other parts of the world  do not cost that amount of time to come  to the same painful understanding that  we need to talk not fight  all right and from our from our virtual  press room we have a question from the  wrath thank you so much thank you thank  you no no we got something much thank  you we have a virtual oppressor oh i'm  so sorry the wrap is coming up sorry  hi kenneth it's joe mcgovern from the  wrap sorry to keep you no worries joe  party um i wanted to ask you know your  it's a beautiful film about a memory you  know um but a half a lifetime ago in  1990  you were first here  as a nominee for directing and acting do  you have any memories from that night  and have you thought about them at all  this evening  m